  "prefLabel": "Ins 3310.01 Review of Action",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Ins 3310.01 Review of Action.\n\n(a) If a consumer believes that any adverse action taken by an insurer violates this chapter or the provisions of RSA 417:4, VIII (g), RSA 417-A, or RSA 417-B, the consumer may request in writing, within 10 days of receipt of the insurer’s or producer’s notice, that the commissioner review the action of the insurer.\n\n(b) If an insurer shall receive confirmation of an inaccuracy in a credit report from a consumer reporting agency, the insurer shall, within 30 days after receipt of the notice and retroactive to the effective date:\n\n(1) Re-underwrite the consumer, if applicable;\n\n(2) Re-rate the consumer's insurance policy; and\n\n(3) Adjust the premium accordingly.\n\nSource. #7658, eff 9-1-02; ss by #8052, eff 7-1-04; ss by #9634, eff 7-1-10; ss by #12599, eff 8-3-18",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/ins3300.html"
